title: 'XZ spatial context: zoom to padded bounding box of edits with square aspect and visible min/max'
updated_at: "2026-09-11T04:09:05Z"
---
The XZ spatial context plot currently renders the whole map extent, so edits become a tiny blob in the middle. Change it to zoom in to a padded bounding box around the actual edits on the XZ grid. Preserve map aspect ratio: the X and Z grid must be square (equal scale per meter), not stretched to a rectangular panel. Optionally arrange the plot at roughly 2/3 of the width and put supplementary info in a side column. The grid must clearly display the min and max values for X and Z (axis tick labels in metres, monospace). Keep existing coverage/marginal-point caveats honest for the zoomed view.